    "q-2930": {
      "dom_id": "step-q2930",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find $\\sqrt{{a}^{2}}$ given that $a>0.$",
      "worked_solution": "The square root of a squared quantity can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nIn our case, we can simplify the given expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{a}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{(a)^{2}} & = \\\\ |a| & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that $a>0,$ and we know that the absolute value of any positive number is just itself, so we have $|a|=a.$ Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a|=a.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
